## Strategic Principles

Principle: Native yield as core differentiator, not add-on
Explanation: Seluruh arsitektur (precompile, escrow, oracle, rebasing) dibangun sekitar native yield sejak genesis. Bukan fitur yang ditambahkan kemudian.
Evidence: NativeYieldPrecompile deployed genesis block【Phase 4 — Core Components】; Launch blog leads with native yield【Phase 1 — Category】; 53.5% token allocation funds yield-seeking behavior【Phase 6 — Distribution】
Supporting Dataset: Phase 1, Phase 4, Phase 6
Confidence: HIGH

Principle: Incentive-first growth over organic adoption
Explanation: Points (user) + Gold (builder) programs drive semua metrics (TVL, tx count, developer activity). Growth budget = 53.5% token supply.
Evidence: Points S1 pre-mainnet Nov 2023【Phase 3 — EV-004】; Gold for builder announced same time【Phase 3 — EV-005】; Allocation 25.5%+28%【Phase 6 — Distribution】; TVL correlates with incentive seasons【Phase 8 — Adoption Metrics】
Supporting Dataset: Phase 3, Phase 6, Phase 8
Confidence: HIGH

Principle: Speed to market > decentralization at launch
Explanation: Centralized sequencer, permissioned proposer/challenger, Foundation multisig upgrade control — semua untuk launch Feb 2024. Decentralization deferred.
Evidence: Single sequencer operated by Foundation【Phase 4 — Core Components】; Permissioned L2OutputOracle/DisputeGame【Phase 4 — Security Model】; No forced inclusion【Phase 4 — Known Technical Limitations】; Phase 9 confirms "Time-to-market priority"【Phase 9 — Decision Timeline】
Supporting Dataset: Phase 4, Phase 9
Confidence: HIGH

Principle: Modular adoption of battle-tested components (OP Stack fault proof) + custom differentiation layer (native yield)
Explanation: Reuse DisputeGame/Cannon dari OP Stack, build custom yield precompile, custom sequencer, custom yield distribution.
Evidence: DisputeGame uses OP Stack Cannon【Phase 4 — Core Components】; NativeYieldPrecompile fully custom【Phase 4 — Core Components】; Phase 9 states "OP Stack fault proof components ready tapi decentralized sequencer/challenger belum mature"【Phase 9 — Decision Timeline】
Supporting Dataset: Phase 4, Phase 9
Confidence: HIGH

Principle: Founder-led ecosystem leverage (Blur integration) untuk cold-start advantage
Explanation: Shared founder (Tieshun) bridge Blur NFT trader base ke Blast. Built-in distribution channel.
Evidence: Tieshun co-founder Blur & Blast【Phase 2 — Entity: Tieshun Roquerre】; Blur listed as external company with Distribution function【Phase 2 — Entity: Blur】; Launch blog mentions Blur integration【Phase 3 — EV-001】
Supporting Dataset: Phase 2, Phase 3
Confidence: HIGH

Principle: Cayman Foundation wrapper untuk legal flexibility dan privacy
Explanation: Jurisdiksi Cayman memungkinkan token issuance, treasury opacity, upgrade control tanpa public disclosure requirements.
Evidence: "Founding Entity: Blast Foundation (Cayman Islands)"【Phase 1 — Founding Entity】; Treasury undisclosed【Phase 5 — Treasury】; Upgrade keys Foundation multisig no timelock【Phase 4 — Security Model】
Supporting Dataset: Phase 1, Phase 4, Phase 5
Confidence: HIGH

Principle: Token emissions sebagai primary growth capital, bukan protocol revenue
Explanation: No meaningful protocol revenue disclosed; sequencer fees small; growth funded by 53.5% token allocation emissions.
Evidence: Revenue Model only lists potential sources【Phase 5 — Revenue Model】; Revenue History "tidak diungkap"【Phase 5 — Revenue History】; Allocation 53.5% incentives【Phase 6 — Distribution】; Phase 9 confirms "Fund ecosystem via Blast Gold (token emissions) bukan grants dalam stablecoin"【Phase 9 — Financial Decision Pattern】
Supporting Dataset: Phase 5, Phase 6, Phase 9
Confidence: HIGH

